# Bible Expert OT Quality Investigation — Key Lessons (2026-06-13)

## Critical Insight: Three Incompatible Morphology Systems in One Codebase

The bible-expert study_html_generator.py uses JS functions (explainEnding, verbTenseEs) that only understand RMAC format (V-AAI-3S). Two other morphology systems in the same DB silently fail:

| System | Format | Example | Used By |
|--------|--------|---------|---------|
| RMAC | `V-AAI-3S` (dash-separated) | NT Greek MorphGNT | Parsed correctly |
| OSHM | `HVqp3ms` (no separators, H prefix) | WLC Hebrew | Falls to generic fallback |
| CATSS | `V.AAI3S` (dot-separated) | LXX Greek | Falls to generic fallback |

Fix for LXX (1 line): `(rmac || '').replace(/\./g, '-')` before any startsWith checks.
Fix for Hebrew: New `explainHebrewMorph(code)` function — strip H/A prefix, split on '/', parse POS+stem+form.

## Ironic Finding: LXX Normalization Fixes NT Bug As Side Effect

RMAC codes like `V-AAI-3S` have an extra dash before person/number that breaks `code[off+3]` (gets '-' instead of person char). LXX codes `V.AAI3S` after dot->dash become `V-AAI3S` — NO extra dash — so `code[3]='3'`, `code[4]='S'` parse correctly. The LXX normalization fix also fixes NT person/number display.

## Dead Code Pattern: Generate Functions Never Wired

`unified_html_generator.py` has 893 lines including `generate_unified_html()` but is never imported in server.py. Always grep for call sites when claiming a generator module is "integrated".

## LXX Variant Book Names Are NOT Standard Aliases

The LXX morphology DB uses text-critical variant codes (JoshA, JoshB, JudgA, JudgB, DanOG, DanTh, BelOG, BelTh, SusOG, SusTh, 1Esdr, 2Esdr) completely absent from books.py. 94,675 LXX words unreachable.

Fix: add each as alias to canonical book in books.py.

## Patristic OT Coverage Contradiction Resolution

c2-kb reported 5,037 OT patristic entries — wrong. Actual: 57,502 OT patristic entries (Psalms: 21,625, Genesis: 9,266, Isaiah: 5,206). Additionally 112,974 entries with book='' are unindexed.

## Hebrew External Links Require Conditional Branching

BibleHub: `/greek/{num}.htm` vs `/hebrew/{num}.htm`. BLB: `/kjv/tr/` for Greek vs `/kjv/wlc/` for Hebrew. Perseus and Logeion are Greek-only — remove for Hebrew, keep STEP Bible (works for both H and G numbers).
